# AI Assistance Disclosure:
# Tool: Codex (model: GPT-6), date: 2026-10-13
# Scope: Exclude secrets, dependencies and obsolete native build artifacts from stock Envoy packaging.
# Author review: Pending Jie Yang's review.
# Tool: Claude Code (model: Claude Opus 5), date: 2026-11-09
# Scope: Excluded Syncthing's *.sync-conflict-* copies from this build context, which the
#   repository-root .dockerignore never reaches because this service builds from its own
#   directory (issue #52).
# Author review: Cole Lin, read and approved.

node_modules
dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.build
envoy/__pycache__

# Syncthing's conflict copies. They sit next to the file they diverged from, so `COPY src` pulls
# them into the image and the build compiles them - and they are older than the file they came
# from, so they fail. The repository-root .dockerignore cannot help here: this service's build
# context is its own directory, so Docker reads this file instead (issue #52).
**/*.sync-conflict-*
